{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 2460 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "8ae42df80da373d4d98fb1f39ac346eb485f92f65c97257d3fc4f916a7ca532e" :edb/db-before-t 2459 :edb/db-after-t 2460 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535772 50 #inst "2026-10-09T06:53:26.515Z" 13194139535772 true] [17592186112318 1000 #edb/ref 17592186365418 13194139535772 true] [17592186115278 1020 #edb/ref 17592186365419 13194139535772 true] [17592186115279 1020 #edb/ref 17592186365422 13194139535772 true] [17592186115280 1020 #edb/ref 17592186365426 13194139535772 true] [17592186115280 1020 #edb/ref 17592186365429 13194139535772 true] [17592186115483 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535772 true] [17592186115483 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070169/assets/6d32c4a97154570f8a66f89ba5fee46f11aa09d2cd152edb4aa05f2613d035f3.png)\n\nGiven that $\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠B)=\\frac{3}{2},$ the **exact** area of $△ABC$ shown above is{{field-1}} square units." 13194139535772 true] [17592186115483 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1608/Source/Images/q-244471.png)\n\nGiven that $\\tan (m∠B) = \\frac{3}{2}$, the **exact** area of $△ABC$ shown above is {{field-1}} square units." 13194139535772 false] [17592186115483 1145 "In this case, the area of the right triangle is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}AC\\cdot BC.\n$$\n\nWe are given that $\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠B)=\\frac{3}{2}.$ Notice that relative to $∠B,$ we have expressions for the lengths of the opposite side $\\overset{―}{AC}$ and adjacent side $\\overset{―}{BC}.$ Hence, we can use the tangent ratio to solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠B) & =\\frac{AC}{BC} \\\\ \\frac{3}{2} & =\\frac{x+3}{3x-5} \\\\ 3(3x-5) & =2(x+3) \\\\ 9x-15 & =2x+6 \\\\ 7x & =21 \\\\ x & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the side lengths are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BC & =3x-5=3(3)-5=4, \\\\ AC & =x+3=3+3=6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $△ABC$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}AC\\cdot BC \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 6\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =12.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535772 true] [17592186365418 1034 "24" 13194139535772 true] [17592186365418 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535772 true] [17592186365418 1111 #uuid "2139b04c-289d-5734-9d0c-3e8fa33c57fa" 13194139535772 true] [17592186365419 1017 #edb/ref 17592186365420 13194139535772 true] [17592186365419 1089 "q-251088" 13194139535772 true] [17592186365419 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535772 true] [17592186365419 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070169/assets/7e555f1574ba37c5b2ac8f4bca54f0d9e2b449e1351f792feba334ddbdc5b8df.png)\n\nGiven that $\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠B)=\\sqrt{3},$ the **exact** area of $△ABC$ shown above is{{field-1}} square units." 13194139535772 true] [17592186365419 1113 #uuid "beadd374-8e12-5792-b24a-a4f724a8512e" 13194139535772 true] [17592186365419 1145 "In this case, the area of the right triangle is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}BC\\cdot AC.\n$$\n\nWe are given that $\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠B)=\\sqrt{3}.$ Notice that relative to $∠B,$ we have expressions for the lengths of the opposite side $\\overset{―}{AC}$ and adjacent side $\\overset{―}{BC}.$ Hence, we can use the tangent ratio to solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠B) & =\\frac{AC}{BC} \\\\ \\sqrt{3} & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}(x-4)}{8-x} \\\\ \\sqrt{3}(8-x) & =\\sqrt{3}(x-4) \\\\ 8-x & =x-4 \\\\ 2x & =12 \\\\ x & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the side lengths are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BC & =8-x=8-6=2, \\\\ AC & =\\sqrt{3}(x-4)=\\sqrt{3}(6-4)=2\\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $△ABC$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}BC\\cdot AC \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 2\\cdot 2\\sqrt{3} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535772 true] [17592186365420 1000 #edb/ref 17592186365421 13194139535772 true] [17592186365420 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535772 true] [17592186365420 1041 "field-1" 13194139535772 true] [17592186365420 1104 #edb/ref 17592186365421 13194139535772 true] [17592186365420 1110 #uuid "64bc7717-0df8-5c78-a857-4cb93574195c" 13194139535772 true] [17592186365421 1034 "2\\sqrt{3}" 13194139535772 true] [17592186365421 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535772 true] [17592186365421 1111 #uuid "42f7b1df-18f4-52ad-9ec3-1d61fe6b9f6b" 13194139535772 true] [17592186365422 1017 #edb/ref 17592186365423 13194139535772 true] [17592186365422 1089 "q-251125" 13194139535772 true] [17592186365422 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535772 true] [17592186365422 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070169/assets/58af9726d81e1d926f814736fa92dc95c427d4346c40252470380f51a5fcf50a.png)\n\nGiven that $\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta =3,$ the **exact** area of $△ABC$ shown above is{{field-1}} square units." 13194139535772 true] [17592186365422 1113 #uuid "c177def7-29b8-599b-97db-32717a8c6daa" 13194139535772 true] [17592186365422 1145 "In this case, the area of the right triangle is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}AC\\cdot BC.\n$$\n\nWe are given that $\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta =3,$ where $\\theta =m∠B.$ Notice we're also given the length of the side $\\overset{―}{AC}$ opposite to $∠B.$ Hence, we can use the tangent ratio to find the length of the adjacent side $\\overset{―}{BC}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{AC}{BC} \\\\ 3 & =\\frac{15}{BC} \\\\ BC & =\\frac{15}{3} \\\\ BC & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $△ABC$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}AC\\cdot BC \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 15\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =37.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535772 true] [17592186365423 1000 #edb/ref 17592186365424 13194139535772 true] [17592186365423 1000 #edb/ref 17592186365425 13194139535772 true] [17592186365423 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535772 true] [17592186365423 1041 "field-1" 13194139535772 true] [17592186365423 1104 #edb/ref 17592186365424 13194139535772 true] [17592186365423 1110 #uuid "623b1ffa-4e8a-5472-8d41-253d5396fe25" 13194139535772 true] [17592186365424 1034 "\\frac{75}{2}" 13194139535772 true] [17592186365424 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535772 true] [17592186365424 1111 #uuid "3ea00450-1e13-5eb3-9eb2-2e2bc0f74026" 13194139535772 true] [17592186365425 1034 "75" 13194139535772 true] [17592186365425 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535772 true] [17592186365425 1111 #uuid "6c2a70e4-b433-5353-a8e9-f37ffb1d55cc" 13194139535772 true] [17592186365426 1017 #edb/ref 17592186365427 13194139535772 true] [17592186365426 1089 "q-251187" 13194139535772 true] [17592186365426 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535772 true] [17592186365426 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070169/assets/d792a93992bbd915063156e0c8fb4f65a71f1609cee5141609e4a5ca6ba6f405.png)\n\nThe **exact** area of $△ABC$ shown above is{{field-1}} square units." 13194139535772 true] [17592186365426 1113 #uuid "39ab6ade-1aec-5997-bc29-3c77858c29a2" 13194139535772 true] [17592186365426 1145 "In this case, the area of the right triangle is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}AB\\cdot BC.\n$$\n\nWe are given that $m∠C={30}^{∘}.$ Notice that relative to $∠C,$ we have expressions for the lengths of the opposite side $\\overset{―}{AB}$ and adjacent side $\\overset{―}{BC}.$ Hence, we can use the tangent ratio to solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠C) & =\\frac{AB}{BC} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡({30}^{∘}) & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}(x-1)}{2x+1} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3} & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}(x-1)}{2x+1} \\\\ \\sqrt{3}(2x+1) & =3\\sqrt{3}(x-1) \\\\ 2x+1 & =3x-3 \\\\ x & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the side lengths are \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =\\sqrt{3}(x-1)=\\sqrt{3}(4-1)=3\\sqrt{3}, \\\\ BC & =2x+1=2(4)+1=9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $△ABC$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot AB\\cdot BC \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 3\\sqrt{3}\\cdot 9 \\\\  & =\\frac{27\\sqrt{3}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535772 true] [17592186365427 1000 #edb/ref 17592186365428 13194139535772 true] [17592186365427 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535772 true] [17592186365427 1041 "field-1" 13194139535772 true] [17592186365427 1104 #edb/ref 17592186365428 13194139535772 true] [17592186365427 1110 #uuid "5cf5abfa-2c94-5664-9ce3-edca82f61bef" 13194139535772 true] [17592186365428 1034 "\\frac{27\\sqrt{3}}{2}" 13194139535772 true] [17592186365428 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535772 true] [17592186365428 1111 #uuid "3ff4e2a3-4a80-52c9-8c6a-07ea2ba2b0b3" 13194139535772 true] [17592186365429 1017 #edb/ref 17592186365430 13194139535772 true] [17592186365429 1089 "q-67571" 13194139535772 true] [17592186365429 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535772 true] [17592186365429 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070169/assets/bb15327593f4452d177ac7d6fbd910c765c847874505b35a13bdd69b123242d0.png)\n\nFind the area (in square units) of $△ABC$ shown above." 13194139535772 true] [17592186365429 1113 #uuid "ba9c7dcd-5197-5b0f-ae7d-9c5a1e5be87f" 13194139535772 true] [17592186365429 1145 "In this case, the area of the right triangle is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}AB\\cdot BC.\n$$\n\nWe are given that $m∠A={45}^{∘}.$ Notice that relative to $∠A,$ we have expressions for the lengths of the opposite side $\\overset{―}{BC}$ and adjacent side $\\overset{―}{AB}.$ Hence, we can use the tangent ratio to solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠A) & =\\frac{BC}{AB} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡({45}^{∘}) & =\\frac{x+3}{2x} \\\\ 1 & =\\frac{x+3}{2x} \\\\ 2x & =x+3 \\\\ x & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the side lengths are \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BC & =x+3=3+3=6, \\\\ AB & =2x=2(3)=6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $△ABC$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot AB\\cdot BC \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 6\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =18.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535772 true] [17592186365430 1000 #edb/ref 17592186365431 13194139535772 true] [17592186365430 10